IF @mode != "generate" AND @mode != "improve"
    RETURN "Estimate writing was not selected."

USE ../../references/be-human.md AS writing_guidance

IF @mode == "generate"
    DO Inspect the affected workflow, relevant code, coverage, and available team
        scoring guidance once. Confirm expected behavior before choosing fixes.
        Use @writing_guidance. Return an object with scope, evidence,
        scope_is_ambiguous, and scoring_guidance. Do not run tests. AS analysis

    IF @analysis.scope_is_ambiguous == TRUE
        DO Clarify only the scope-changing ambiguity from relevant Jira comments
            and attachments. Request outside-sandbox execution on the first Jira
            call and stop if denied or unavailable. Return the clarified scope. AS scope
    ELSE
        SET scope = @analysis.scope

    DO Assess @scope using @analysis.evidence and @analysis.scoring_guidance.
        Return an object with estimate_is_blocked, missing_information,
        assumptions, and material_risks. Further searches must affect the
        estimate. AS assessment

    IF @assessment.estimate_is_blocked == TRUE
        ASK "What is the missing scope or behavior needed for this estimate?" AS clarification

        DO Apply @clarification to @scope and @assessment. Return an updated
            assessment whose estimate_is_blocked field is FALSE when enough
            information exists. AS assessment

        IF @assessment.estimate_is_blocked == TRUE
            RETURN "Estimate generation stopped because required information is still missing."

    DO Create the complete in-memory estimate draft for @ticket_id using @scope,
        @analysis.evidence, @assessment, and @writing_guidance. Preserve supported
        developer decisions and the six-row Markdown structure. Use nonnegative
        integer team scores, falling back to 0 for no meaningful work and 1–3
        for increasing complexity. Keep uncertainty in Risk & Unknowns, explain
        zeros, avoid double-counting, calculate the six-score total, and use a
        supported numeric Final Estimate ending in SP without inventing a
        score-to-SP formula. Return the draft string. AS draft

    DO Verify @draft has all required fields, no placeholders or unsupported
        claims, correct row order, valid scores and total, categorized reasons,
        and a supported numeric Final Estimate ending in SP.

IF @mode == "improve"
    DO Refine only the parts of @saved_estimate requested by @request using
        @writing_guidance. Preserve supported decisions, layout, and unrequested
        content. Wording-only edits must not change scores, scope, or SP. Inspect
        evidence only as needed; do not retrieve Jira, investigate code, or run
        tests solely for wording. Return an object with draft,
        unrelated_incomplete_fields, and justified_sp_changes. AS refinement

    SET draft = @refinement.draft

    DO Verify changed fields and dependent totals in @draft are complete and
        supported. Preserve six rows, order, and fields; use nonnegative integer
        scores, explain zeros, keep reasons and uncertainty in their categories,
        avoid double-counting, calculate the correct total, and retain a
        supported numeric Final Estimate ending in SP without invented formulas.

DO Read the first heading from @ticket_path and return only its ticket ID. AS current_ticket_id

IF @current_ticket_id != @ticket_id
    RETURN "Estimate writing stopped because the active ticket changed."

DO Save @draft only to @estimate_path.

DO Verify @estimate_path once against @draft.

PRINT Report @ticket_id, the saved SP, @estimate_path, assumptions, unrelated gaps, and justified SP changes briefly.
